  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Crystal directions and sizes, frost patch shape and drifting flakes vary per cast. The 120 ms reach, the freeze moment and the shatter at 1050 ms stay fixed so a freeze status can sync to them."
  },
  "director_notes": "A freezing ray that leaves the target encased. Choices: (1) the ray is the new beam style ice (slow flow, hard white core, glassy rim, frost drifting off) so it reads cold and solid next to the energy and water beams; (2) the hit is ice crystal spikes (sparks look shard) that freeze in place and hold for the whole contact, then shatter on a fixed frame with a shatter cue, which a game can sync with breaking a freeze status; (3) a frost decal grows under the target and outlives the spell. Palette is pale cyan with white, no saturated blue, so it doesn't read as water."
}
